# Wave W17-S (Route 127): kelp rock — frond-hung rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a green-grey shore rock with kelp fronds hanging from its crown into the sea, foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: the kelp forest walls the trench\u2019s east side through the water — its outlying rocks wear the forest on their crowns). Route 127\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s only frond-hung rock: split from Route 128\u2019s warm-seamed cavern-ring rock and Route 129\u2019s shadow-side lee rock by the hanging green itself.
